-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you Airbnb a property in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Only in the right zone. Surfside permits short-term rentals (under 30 days) in the R3 high-density and C3 commercial districts and restricts or prohibits them in inland R1 low-density zones. A town STR permit and safety inspection are required.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Surfside Beach a golf-cart town?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. Golf carts are a primary local mode of transport, and South Carolina allows registered carts on secondary roads during daylight within a few miles of home.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Why do Surfside Beach median prices look so high?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Because the blended median mixes small inland condos with oceanfront homes. Detached single-family medians run much higher than the overall home-value index, so compare within a tier.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are property taxes on a second home in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In Surfside Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3.1 times a primary home's on the same house.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Public schools fall within Horry County Schools, generally Lakewood Elementary, St. James Intermediate, and St. James High. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Why is Surfside Beach called the family beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It has a quieter, more residential feel than central Myrtle Beach, with steady seasonal demand and a mix of homes and condominiums.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What does Surfside Beach offer investors?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A calmer setting close to the main attractions, with both single-family and condominium options.</p></div></div></section>
